{
  "schema": "br-qbhs0 publication-variant diagnostics v1",
  "bead": "br-qbhs0",
  "host": "thinkstation1 (64 cores), same host and session per block",
  "background": "nopub (skip the per-commit PASSIVE checkpoint and the retirement it triggers; publish only when the WAL exceeds journal_size_limit) won the paced send A/B (pooled p2 p50 0.575x, p90 0.619x) but regressed the release-smoke soak in both orders (reads -16..-21%, fetch_inbox p99 +80%). These runs asked why.",
  "binaries": {
    "base": "2dd72851, build19/base3, am sha256 c5c84438...",
    "nopub": "2dd72851 + nopub_v1.patch, build25/nopub, am 1401e554...",
    "nopub_1mib": "the nopub binary run with DB_JOURNAL_SIZE_LIMIT_BYTES=1048576 (env wrapper)",
    "v1_throttle": "nopub + publication throttled to at most once per 100 ms, build27/v1throttle, am 3051f56d...",
    "v2_retire": "nopub + retire the writer connection after every commit (no checkpoint), build27/v2retire, am 0a597ca4..."
  },
  "rules": {
    "diag_v1v2_plan": "DIAGNOSTIC (mechanism finding, not a landing decision). Written 2026-10-13 ~00:55Z, before builds or runs.\nQuestion: why does nopub (no per-commit checkpoint) regress the release-smoke soak?\n  Observed: reads -16..-21%, fetch_inbox p99 +80% in both orders.\n  At a 1 MiB limit it is worse: reset-gate overhead on most commits.\nV1 (throttled): nopub + publish (PASSIVE + retire-on-deferral, as base) at most every 100 ms.\n  If soak recovers, the regression comes from leaving frames un-backfilled.\nV2 (retire-only): nopub + retire the writer after every commit, with no checkpoint.\n  If soak recovers, the regression comes from long-lived connections.\nRuns: release smoke with the swarm skipped, each variant vs base (build19/base3), both orders.\nReadout: soak reads and fetch_inbox p99 vs base.\n  \"Recovers\" = within 10% of base reads and fetch p99 <= 1.2x base, in both orders.\nWhichever variant recovers (if any) gets a separate pre-registered confirmation A/B before any landing.\n",
    "v2_confirm_rule": "V2 confirmation (br-qbhs0). Written 2026-10-13 ~04:50Z, before any confirmation run.\n\nBackground:\n- nopub (no per-commit checkpoint, no retirement) gave large paced send gains: saturated p50 0.575x, p90 0.619x.\n  But it regressed the release-smoke soak in both orders: reads -16..-21%, fetch_inbox p99 +80%.\n- Diagnostics without the swarm phase (diag_v2v1):\n  - A 1 MiB checkpoint threshold is worse.\n  - V1 (publication throttled to 100 ms) keeps the regression: reads -18%, p99 1.84x.\n  - V2 (no checkpoint, but retire the writer after every commit, as the old per-commit deferral did for 96% of\n    commits under load) mostly recovers: reads -2% / -6%, fetch p99 1.05x / 1.69x.\n- Mechanism: reads slow down on long-lived FrankenSQLite connections; writer retirement was masking that.\n\nCandidate V2 = 2dd72851 + nopub_v1.patch + diag_rc1012m.patch (build27/v2retire, sha 0a597ca4).\nBase = build19/base3 (2dd72851, sha c5c84438).\n\nRuns (same host, one session):\n  P. paced_swarm.py (error payloads recorded), 60 agents, 300 s, WAL sampled:\n     period 2 s: base v2 v2 base base v2; period 6 s: v2 base base v2.\n  R. Full release smoke (with the swarm phase), both orders: v2_vs_base, then base_vs_v2.\n\nDecision:\n  S1 (primary). Pooled P2 send p50 and p90 for v2 <= 0.85x base.\n  G1. Pooled P6 send p50 and p90 <= 1.05x base.\n  G2 (soak). In EACH smoke order, v2 soak reads >= 0.90x base and soak fetch_inbox p99 <= 1.3x base.\n  G3. Every acknowledged id survives SIGKILL (crash and swarm) for v2. Swarm 30 s timeouts for v2 <= base + 5 in each\n      order. Paced errors <= base + 5 at P2 and base + 3 at P6, with no visibility signature in the payloads.\n  G4. Paced WAL peak median <= 1.5x base.\n  C. db lib full, tools it and conformance pass on the V2 code (gated before landing; the C3 visibility test still\n     applies).\n\nWIN only if S1, G1-G4 and C hold. A win goes to the owner before landing, because the publication contract changes.\nOtherwise LOSS, reported, not landed.\n"
  },
